1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,900
It calls it the booth that launched a $1 trillion company.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:09,180
At the party, the boss of that company put on an apron, balanced 10 plates up his arm, and served the tables.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,460
Still remember how?

4
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,520
Dishes first.

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:16,440
Two years later, NVIDIA became the first company ever worth $5 trillion.

6
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,320
Every dollar the three of them put into that booth had become about $8 billion.

7
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:26,500
The kid who scrubbed the toilets in Kentucky now holds the key to artificial intelligence.

8
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,920
And when he talks about who should be allowed to buy his chips, Washington listens.

9
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,820
Every AI lab on Earth needs this man.

10
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,620
Then so do we.

11
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,780
That made him the one man China needed most.

12
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:44,470
October 2022, Washington calls NVIDIA.

13
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:47,770
Your best AI chips can't be sold to China anymore.

14
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:50,230
And the slower ones we made just for China?

15
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:51,850
Those too, China.

16
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:57,130
$17 billion a year, 13% of everything we sell.

17
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:57,710
Was.

18
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,290
How many chips do we need?

19
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:00,710
For a real AI?

20
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:02,170
Tens of thousands.

21
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:03,530
And one costs?

22
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:05,170
About $30,000.

23
00:01:05,910 --> 00:01:07,550
A new car per chip.

24
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:09,130
And how many can we buy?

25
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:09,770
Zero.

26
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:15,770
By Jensen's own account, NVIDIA's share of China's market went from 95% to zero.

27
00:01:16,090 --> 00:01:17,650
And he told Washington so every chance he

